        {
          "published_at": "2026-10-13T18:22:28.164Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/thorstenball/status/2110073700645273771",
          "topic": "How coding agents change software design tradeoffs",
          "text": "There seem to be two groups:\n\n1. Better-is-better group believes that agents finally make the better-is-better solutions happen. Formal methods, static types, Nix, ...\n\n2. Worse-is-better group believes agents will make worse-is-better solution happen because with agents they're no longer worse. Dynamic type systems, bash scripts over neat DSLs, agents running tests dynamically, ...\n\nQuite funny to see",
          "quote_tweet": null,
          "author_replies": [],
          "render_audit": {
            "root_article_url": "https://x.com/thorstenball/status/2110073700645273771",
